    {
      "window_id": "2025.acl-long.1495::appendix::E",
      "paper_id": "2025.acl-long.1495",
      "section_number": "E",
      "section_title": "implementation details and risk considerations",
      "normalized_section_title": "implementation details and risk considerations",
      "window_text": "All results are obtained from a single training run per model, a choice dictated by computational limits but sufficient to demonstrate the method's promise; future work should repeat the experiments with multiple seeds to establish variance. We relied on commercial LLMs, such as GPT4o and Claude, only for polishing language use, with all scientific design and analysis performed by the authors. Although the reported metrics are promising, generated teaching references and dialogues can still contain errors. DDxTutor should therefore be used under the supervision of qualified educators, who can correct inaccuracies and emphasize that the system is a supplementary aid, not a replacement for independent hypothesis-driven medical thinking.",
